<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<pddoc xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" version="1.0">
    <object name="hw.rpi.pwm">
        <title>hw.rpi.pwm</title>
        <meta>
            <authors>
                <author>Serge Poltavsky</author>
            </authors>
            <description>Hardware PWM output for RaspberryPi</description>
            <license>GPL3 or later</license>
            <library>ceammc</library>
            <category>hw</category>
            <keywords>pwm hawdware rpi raspberry</keywords>
            <since>0.9.9</since>
        </meta>
        <info>
            <par>|| Versions &lt;5.0</par>
            <par>The BCM283x SoC supports 2 hardware PWM channels. By default, the channels are
            mapped as follows:</par>
            <par>• PWM0 = GPIO12/GPIO18</par>
            <par>• PWM1 = GPIO13/GPIO19</par>
            <par>Consult the official documentation on how to enable and configure these.</par>
            <par>Note: the Raspberry Pi?s analog audio output uses both PWM channels. Playing audio
            and simultaneously accessing a PWM channel may cause issues.</par>
            <par>~</par>
            <par>|| Raspberry Pi 5 and later</par>
            <par>The Raspberry Pi 5 support 4 hardware PWM channels. By default, the channels are
            mapped as follows:</par>
            <par>• PWM0 = GPIO12</par>
            <par>• PWM1 = GPIO13</par>
            <par>• PWM2 = GPIO18</par>
            <par>• PWM3 = GPIO19</par>
            <par>Consult the official documentation on how to enable and configure these.</par>
            <par>~</par>
            <par>Some of the GPIO pins capable of supporting hardware PWM can also be configured
            for use with other peripherals. Be careful not to enable two peripherals on the same
            pin at the same time.</par>
        </info>
        <methods>
            <method name="polarity">set output polarity 
            <param name="INVERTED" type="bool" required="true">new value. If true: polarity is
            inverted</param></method>
            <method name="freq">set frequency 
            <param name="FREQ" type="float" minvalue="0" units="hertz" required="true">
            frequency</param>
            <param name="DUTY" type="float" minvalue="0" maxvalue="1" required="true">duty
            cycle</param></method>
            <method name="pwm">set period and pulse width. Expected width&lt;=pulse. 
            <param name="PERIOD" type="float" minvalue="0" units="msec" required="true">the whole
            cycle period</param>
            <param name="WIDTH" type="float" minvalue="0" units="msec" required="true">pulse
            width</param></method>
            <method name="period">set period. Expected width&lt;=pulse. 
            <param name="PERIOD" type="float" minvalue="0" units="msec" required="true">the whole
            cycle period</param></method>
            <method name="width">set pulse width. Expected width&lt;=pulse. 
            <param name="WIDTH" type="float" minvalue="0" units="msec" required="true">pulse
            width</param></method>
            <method name="enable">enable PWM. By default it is disabled. 
            <param name="ENABLE" type="bool" required="true">value</param></method>
            <method name="duty">set duty cycle 
            <param name="DUTY" type="float" minvalue="0" maxvalue="1" required="true">duty
            cycle</param></method>
        </methods>
        <arguments>
            <argument name="CH" type="int" minvalue="-1" maxvalue="3">PWM channel. See
            @ch</argument>
        </arguments>
        <properties>
            <property name="@ch" type="int" default="-1" minvalue="-1" maxvalue="3"
            access="initonly">PWM channel. Valid values are: 0-3. If equals -1: no PWM channel
            selected.</property>
        </properties>
        <inlets>
            <inlet>
                <xinfo>input messages</xinfo>
            </inlet>
        </inlets>
        <outlets>
            <outlet>no output</outlet>
        </outlets>
        <example>
            <pdascii>
<![CDATA[
[T] /*should be called after setting PWM!*/
|
[enable $1 #a(


  [ui.hsl #b]        [ui.hsl #d]
  |                  |
  [freq $1 0.5 #c(   [pwm 20 $1 #e(


[hw.rpi.pwm @ch 0 #x]
[X a->x] [X c->x] [X e->x]
#b @show_value 1 @min 50 @max 500
#d @show_value 1 @min 0 @max 20
]]>
            </pdascii>
        </example>
    </object>
</pddoc>
